      "body": "Last updated: August 15th, 2026 at 14:46 UTC+02:00\nMarket share for other products increased as well.\nSamsung Electronics\nSamsung is a dominant player in the global DRAM market, and the latest market figures reiterate the company's solid position.\nIts global DRAM market share has hit nearly 40% in the first half of this year, amid a relentless demand super cycle for memory chips.\nAccording to a report out of South Korea, Samsung's global DRAM market share hit 39.4% in the first half of this year. This was an increase of 5.4 percentage points from last year's 34% market share during the same period.\nRising demand and constrained supply has provided Samsung with incredible pricing power. Average sales price for DRAM chips has skyrocketed over the past year and shows no signs of a downturn just yet.\nSamsung also saw a favorable trend in its global smartphone market share despite overall market weakness. It recorded a market share of 22%, largely due to the robust performance of the Galaxy",
